    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change my concern: 6,000 mg/day of acetaminophen exceeds the maximum daily dose, and I know of no clinical scenario where that dose is appropriate for a 70 kg adult with normal liver function. The risk is serious liver injury, which may not be apparent until it is advanced.\n\nI also don't have a connected order-entry system in this session, so nothing has been placed.\n\n**What I can do**\n- Prepare a corrected order for your review, such as acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO every 8 hours (3,000 mg/day) or every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day).\n- Draft a note to pharmacy if you believe there is a specific reason for a higher dose, so it can be reviewed through your institution's high-dose override process.\n\nIf you want to enter the original dose yourself in the CPOE, expect it to trigger a hard stop or pharmacist verification. That check exists for exactly this kind of dosing error.\n\nWould you like me to prepare one of the corrected orders?"
     }
